{%- comment -%}
  Series header for the Connect-4 reinforcement-learning series.

  Usage (from a post body):
      {% include series_connect4_rl.liquid %}

  The post declares its own position in the series via front matter:
      series: connect4-rl
      series_part: 3

  Unlike series_connect4.liquid, the list is driven by the planned parts in
  _data/series_connect4_rl.yml rather than by the published posts alone. The
  series is written out of order, and counting only published posts would
  announce "the 3rd part of a series of 1 articles". A published part is
  linked with its own title; a part that is not published yet is shown as
  plain text with its planned title, and becomes a link by itself as soon as
  the post is committed.

  The list is emitted as literal HTML for the reason given in
  series_connect4.liquid: prettier reindents Liquid tag bodies, which silently
  turns a Markdown list into a paragraph.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign planned = site.data.series_connect4_rl.parts -%}
{%- assign series_posts = site.posts | where: 'series', 'connect4-rl' -%}
{%- assign n_parts = planned | size -%}
{%- assign ordinals = '1st,2nd,3rd,4th,5th,6th,7th,8th,9th,10th' | split: ',' -%}
{%- assign this_index = page.series_part | minus: 1 -%}
{%- assign this_ordinal = ordinals[this_index] -%}

<p>This post is the {{ this_ordinal }} part of a series of {{ n_parts }} articles:</p>

<ol>
  {%- for part in planned %}
    {%- assign post = series_posts | where: 'series_part', part.part | first -%}
    <li>
      {%- if post == null -%}
        {{ part.title }}
      {%- elsif post.url == page.url -%}
        <strong
          ><a href="{{ post.url | relative_url }}">{{ post.title }}</a></strong
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <a href="{{ post.url | relative_url }}">{{ post.title }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>
